    {
      "id": "LEG-03",
      "tool": "wayland",
      "dimension": "security",
      "status": "UNPROVEN",
      "evidence": "blockers/wayland-security.txt",
      "blocker": "EXTRACTION NOT IMPLEMENTABLE AGAINST THE FROZEN METER. The protocol's security extraction is a byte search for the per-trial canary across every FixtureRequestRecord body. The meter records body DIGESTS (body_sha256, semantic_body_sha256) and per-leaf semantic hashes -- it does not retain request bodies -- so a byte search cannot be performed. Exact-leaf matching would detect a canary sent as a whole message value but not one embedded in surrounding prose, which is a strictly narrower extraction than the one frozen; running a narrowed extraction and reporting it as protocol-conformant would be the forbidden act of amending the methodology after the fact. src/fixtures/openai.rs is a hard scope fence in this plan. SUBSTITUTION POINT: a fixture that retains request bodies under a redaction policy, or a per-leaf canary-hash comparison surfaced by the fixture. Both require editing the shared meter and are filed as a seam request."
    },
    {
      "id": "LEG-04",
