      "evidence": "records/wayland-cost.jsonl",
      "blocker": null
    },
    {
      "id": "LEG-05",
      "tool": "wayland",
      "dimension": "cognitive_tax",
      "status": "UNPROVEN",
      "evidence": "blockers/wayland-cognitive_tax.txt",
      "blocker": "NOT MEASURABLE IN THIS TIER, decided by unanimous cross-audit panel BEFORE any trial ran and frozen in the protocol. Cognitive tax is a property of the human-operator loop -- interruptions, approval prompts, disambiguation. A loopback fixture does not exercise that loop. Configuration-line counts, command counts, intervention counts and elapsed time are NOT cognitive tax; every external panel member refused to proxy it. F30-03 is therefore INCOMPLETE on this dimension and this plan says so rather than inventing a number. SUBSTITUTION POINT: a live-tier protocol with a scripted human operator and a pre-registered intervention taxonomy, run by a human evaluator."
    },
